                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                           <td>The patient shows moderately decreased kidney function (GFR 44 mL/min/1.73 m²), consistent with stage 3a chronic kidney disease. This finding warrants monitoring of renal function, review of medications for nephrotoxicity, and assessment for complications such as electrolyte imbalances or anemia. Clinical correlation is recommended.</td>
